const t=[{id:"act-faith",title:"Act of Faith",tags:["basic","faith","daily"],text:"O my God, I firmly believe that thou art one God in three divine Persons, Father, Son, and Holy Ghost; I believe that thy divine Son became man, and died for our sins, and that he will come to judge the living and the dead. I believe these and all the truths which the Holy Catholic Church teaches, because thou hast revealed them, who canst neither deceive nor be deceived. Amen."},{id:"act-hope",title:"Act of Hope",tags:["basic","faith","trust","daily"],text:"O my God, relying on thy almighty power and infinite mercy and promises, I hope to gain pardon of my sins, the help of thy grace, and life everlasting, through the merits of Jesus Christ, my Lord and Redeemer. Amen."},{id:"act-charity",title:"Act of Love",tags:["basic","faith","daily"],text:"O my God, I love thee above all things, with my whole heart and soul, because thou art all-good and worthy of all love. I love my neighbor as myself for the love of thee. I forgive all who have injured me, and I ask pardon of all whom I have injured. Amen."},{id:"regina-caeli",title:"Regina Caeli",tags:["mary","easter","praise","daily"],note:"Prayed in place of the Angelus through the Easter season.",text:`O Queen of heaven, rejoice, alleluia: for he whom thou didst merit to bear, alleluia, hath risen as he said, alleluia. Pray for us to God, alleluia.

V. Rejoice and be glad, O Virgin Mary, alleluia.
R. For the Lord hath risen indeed, alleluia.

Let us pray. O God, who gave joy to the world through the resurrection of thy Son our Lord Jesus Christ, grant, we beseech thee, that through the intercession of the Virgin Mary, his Mother, we may attain the joys of everlasting life. Through the same Christ our Lord. Amen.`},{id:"sub-tuum",title:"Sub tuum praesidium",tags:["mary","protection","trouble","intercession"],note:"One of the oldest prayers to Mary known, found on an Egyptian papyrus of about the third century.",text:"We fly to thy patronage, O holy Mother of God; despise not our petitions in our necessities, but deliver us always from all dangers, O glorious and blessed Virgin. Amen."},{id:"benedictus",title:"The Benedictus (Canticle of Zechariah)",tags:["morning","praise","thanksgiving","lauds"],note:"Luke 1:68-79 in the traditional Douay-Rheims wording; prayed every morning in the Divine Office.",text:`Blessed be the Lord God of Israel; because he hath visited and wrought the redemption of his people: and hath raised up an horn of salvation to us, in the house of David his servant: as he spoke by the mouth of his holy prophets, who are from the beginning: salvation from our enemies, and from the hand of all that hate us: to perform mercy to our fathers, and to remember his holy testament, the oath which he swore to Abraham our father, that he would grant to us, that being delivered from the hand of our enemies, we may serve him without fear, in holiness and justice before him, all our days.

And thou, child, shalt be called the prophet of the Highest: for thou shalt go before the face of the Lord to prepare his ways: to give knowledge of salvation to his people, unto the remission of their sins: through the bowels of the mercy of our God, in which the Orient from on high hath visited us: to enlighten them that sit in darkness, and in the shadow of death: to direct our feet into the way of peace.`},{id:"nunc-dimittis",title:"The Nunc Dimittis (Canticle of Simeon)",tags:["evening","dead","peace","compline","thanksgiving"],note:"Luke 2:29-32 in the traditional wording; prayed every night at Compline.",text:"Now thou dost dismiss thy servant, O Lord, according to thy word in peace; because my eyes have seen thy salvation, which thou hast prepared before the face of all peoples: a light to the revelation of the Gentiles, and the glory of thy people Israel."},{id:"psalm-91",title:"Psalm 91: He that dwelleth in the secret place",tags:["anxiety","protection","trust","fear","evening"],note:"King James wording. Numbered Psalm 90 in the Greek and Latin Bibles.",text:`He that dwelleth in the secret place of the most High shall abide under the shadow of the Almighty. I will say of the Lord, He is my refuge and my fortress: my God; in him will I trust.

Surely he shall deliver thee from the snare of the fowler, and from the noisome pestilence. He shall cover thee with his feathers, and under his wings shalt thou trust: his truth shall be thy shield and buckler. Thou shalt not be afraid for the terror by night; nor for the arrow that flieth by day.

Because thou hast made the Lord, which is my refuge, even the most High, thy habitation; there shall no evil befall thee, neither shall any plague come nigh thy dwelling. For he shall give his angels charge over thee, to keep thee in all thy ways. They shall bear thee up in their hands, lest thou dash thy foot against a stone.

Because he hath set his love upon me, therefore will I deliver him: I will set him on high, because he hath known my name. He shall call upon me, and I will answer him: I will be with him in trouble; I will deliver him, and honour him. With long life will I satisfy him, and shew him my salvation.`},{id:"psalm-121",title:"Psalm 121: I will lift up mine eyes",tags:["travel","trust","protection","anxiety","evening"],note:"King James wording. Numbered Psalm 120 in the Greek and Latin Bibles.",text:`I will lift up mine eyes unto the hills, from whence cometh my help. My help cometh from the Lord, which made heaven and earth.

He will not suffer thy foot to be moved: he that keepeth thee will not slumber. Behold, he that keepeth Israel shall neither slumber nor sleep.

The Lord is thy keeper: the Lord is thy shade upon thy right hand. The sun shall not smite thee by day, nor the moon by night.

The Lord shall preserve thee from all evil: he shall preserve thy soul. The Lord shall preserve thy going out and thy coming in from this time forth, and even for evermore.`},{id:"aaronic",title:"The Lord bless thee and keep thee",tags:["blessing","family","evening","daily"],note:"Numbers 6:24-26, the priestly blessing, in the Douay-Rheims wording. Parents bless their children with it.",text:"The Lord bless thee, and keep thee. The Lord shew his face to thee, and have mercy on thee. The Lord turn his countenance to thee, and give thee peace."},{id:"humility",title:"Litany of Humility",tags:["humility","confession","temptation","sorrow"],note:"By Rafael Cardinal Merry del Val (1865–1930), secretary of state to St Pius X.",text:`O Jesus, meek and humble of heart, hear me.
From the desire of being esteemed, deliver me, Jesus.
From the desire of being loved, deliver me, Jesus.
From the desire of being extolled, deliver me, Jesus.
From the desire of being honored, deliver me, Jesus.
From the desire of being praised, deliver me, Jesus.
From the desire of being preferred to others, deliver me, Jesus.
From the desire of being consulted, deliver me, Jesus.
From the desire of being approved, deliver me, Jesus.
From the fear of being humiliated, deliver me, Jesus.
From the fear of being despised, deliver me, Jesus.
From the fear of suffering rebukes, deliver me, Jesus.
From the fear of being calumniated, deliver me, Jesus.
From the fear of being forgotten, deliver me, Jesus.
From the fear of being ridiculed, deliver me, Jesus.
From the fear of being wronged, deliver me, Jesus.
From the fear of being suspected, deliver me, Jesus.

That others may be loved more than I, Jesus, grant me the grace to desire it.
That others may be esteemed more than I, Jesus, grant me the grace to desire it.
That, in the opinion of the world, others may increase and I may decrease, Jesus, grant me the grace to desire it.
That others may be chosen and I set aside, Jesus, grant me the grace to desire it.
That others may be praised and I unnoticed, Jesus, grant me the grace to desire it.
That others may be preferred to me in everything, Jesus, grant me the grace to desire it.
That others may become holier than I, provided that I may become as holy as I should, Jesus, grant me the grace to desire it.`},{id:"teresa-bookmark",title:"Let nothing disturb thee",tags:["anxiety","trust","peace","fear"],note:"Written by St Teresa of Ávila in her breviary; this is Longfellow’s translation.",text:`Let nothing disturb thee,
Let nothing affright thee,
All things are passing;
God never changeth;
Patient endurance
Attaineth to all things;
Who God possesseth
In nothing is wanting;
Alone God sufficeth.`},{id:"late-have-i-loved",title:"Late have I loved thee",tags:["sorrow","confession","conversion","thanksgiving"],note:"St Augustine, Confessions 10.27, put into plain English from the older translations.",text:`Late have I loved thee, O Beauty so ancient and so new; late have I loved thee! For behold, thou wert within me, and I outside; and I sought thee outside, and in my unloveliness fell upon those lovely things that thou hast made. Thou wert with me, and I was not with thee. Those things held me back from thee, which would not have been at all unless they were in thee.

Thou didst call and cry aloud, and thou didst burst my deafness. Thou didst flash and shine, and thou didst chase away my blindness. Thou didst breathe fragrance, and I drew in breath and I pant for thee. I tasted, and I hunger and thirst. Thou didst touch me, and I burned for thy peace.`},{id:"lead-kindly-light",title:"Lead, kindly Light",tags:["trust","guidance","decision","anxiety","evening"],note:"John Henry Newman, written at sea in 1833, years before he became a Catholic.",text:`Lead, kindly Light, amid the encircling gloom,
Lead thou me on!
The night is dark, and I am far from home;
Lead thou me on!
Keep thou my feet; I do not ask to see
The distant scene; one step enough for me.

I was not ever thus, nor prayed that thou
Shouldst lead me on;
I loved to choose and see my path; but now
Lead thou me on!
I loved the garish day, and, spite of fears,
Pride ruled my will: remember not past years.

So long thy power hath blest me, sure it still
Will lead me on,
O’er moor and fen, o’er crag and torrent, till
The night is gone,
And with the morn those angel faces smile,
Which I have loved long since, and lost awhile.`},{id:"newman-mission",title:"God has created me to do him some definite service",tags:["vocation","trust","guidance","decision","sick"],note:"From Newman’s Meditations and Devotions (1893).",text:`God has created me to do him some definite service; he has committed some work to me which he has not committed to another. I have my mission. I may never know it in this life, but I shall be told it in the next.

I am a link in a chain, a bond of connexion between persons. He has not created me for naught. I shall do good, I shall do his work; I shall be an angel of peace, a preacher of truth in my own place, while not intending it, if I do but keep his commandments and serve him in my calling.

Therefore I will trust him. Whatever, wherever I am, I can never be thrown away. If I am in sickness, my sickness may serve him; in perplexity, my perplexity may serve him; if I am in sorrow, my sorrow may serve him. He does nothing in vain. He knows what he is about.`},{id:"mercier",title:"Prayer to the Holy Spirit (Cardinal Mercier)",tags:["holy-spirit","guidance","decision","study"],note:"Désiré-Joseph Mercier (1851–1926), Archbishop of Mechelen.",text:"O Holy Spirit, beloved of my soul, I adore thee. Enlighten me, guide me, strengthen me, console me. Tell me what I should do; give me thy orders. I promise to submit myself to all that thou desirest of me and to accept all that thou permittest to happen to me. Let me only know thy will."},{id:"ignatius-generosity",title:"Prayer for generosity",tags:["work","vocation","offering","service"],note:"Attributed to St Ignatius of Loyola.",text:"Lord, teach me to be generous; teach me to serve thee as thou deservest; to give and not to count the cost, to fight and not to heed the wounds, to toil and not to seek for rest, to labor and not to ask for reward, save that of knowing that I do thy will. Amen."},{id:"richard-chichester",title:"Thanks be to thee, my Lord Jesus Christ",tags:["thanksgiving","evening","daily"],note:"St Richard of Chichester (1197–1253).",text:"Thanks be to thee, my Lord Jesus Christ, for all the benefits and blessings which thou hast given me, for all the pains and insults which thou hast borne for me. O most merciful Redeemer, Friend and Brother, may I know thee more clearly, love thee more dearly, and follow thee more nearly, day by day. Amen."},{id:"patrick-christ-with-me",title:"Christ with me (from St Patrick’s Breastplate)",tags:["protection","morning","travel","fear","trust"],note:"From the Lorica attributed to St Patrick, in Kuno Meyer’s 1911 translation.",text:"Christ with me, Christ before me, Christ behind me, Christ in me, Christ beneath me, Christ above me, Christ on my right, Christ on my left, Christ when I lie down, Christ when I sit down, Christ when I arise, Christ in the heart of every man who thinks of me, Christ in the mouth of every man who speaks of me, Christ in every eye that sees me, Christ in every ear that hears me."},{id:"en-ego",title:"Before a crucifix (En ego)",tags:["confession","sorrow","lent","eucharist"],note:"A prayer after Communion, with a plenary indulgence long attached to it on Fridays in Lent.",text:"Behold, O kind and most sweet Jesus, I cast myself upon my knees in thy sight, and with the most fervent desire of my soul I pray and beseech thee that thou wouldst impress upon my heart lively sentiments of faith, hope and charity, with true repentance for my sins and a firm desire of amendment, while with deep affection and grief of soul I ponder within myself and mentally contemplate thy five most precious wounds, having before my eyes that which David the prophet said of thee, O good Jesus: “They have pierced my hands and my feet, they have numbered all my bones.”"},{id:"o-sacrament",title:"O Sacrament most holy",tags:["eucharist","praise","thanksgiving","adoration"],text:"O Sacrament most holy, O Sacrament divine, all praise and all thanksgiving be every moment thine."},{id:"sign-latin",title:"Sign of the Cross (Latin)",tags:["latin","basic"],text:"In nómine Patris, et Fílii, et Spíritus Sancti. Amen."},{id:"pater-latin",title:"Pater noster (Latin)",tags:["latin","basic","lord"],text:"Pater noster, qui es in cælis, sanctificétur nomen tuum; advéniat regnum tuum; fiat volúntas tua, sicut in cælo et in terra. Panem nostrum quotidiánum da nobis hódie; et dimítte nobis débita nostra, sicut et nos dimíttimus debitóribus nostris; et ne nos indúcas in tentationem; sed líbera nos a malo. Amen."},{id:"ave-latin",title:"Ave Maria (Latin)",tags:["latin","basic","mary"],text:"Ave María, grátia plena, Dóminus tecum. Benedícta tu in muliéribus, et benedíctus fructus ventris tui, Iesus. Sancta María, Mater Dei, ora pro nobis peccatóribus, nunc et in hora mortis nostræ. Amen."},{id:"gloria-latin",title:"Gloria Patri (Latin)",tags:["latin","basic","trinity"],text:"Glória Patri, et Fílio, et Spirítui Sancto. Sicut erat in princípio, et nunc, et semper, et in sǽcula sæculórum. Amen."},{id:"salve-latin",title:"Salve Regina (Latin)",tags:["latin","mary","evening"],text:"Salve, Regína, Mater misericórdiæ; vita, dulcédo, et spes nostra, salve. Ad te clamámus, éxsules fílii Hevæ. Ad te suspirámus, geméntes et flentes in hac lacrimárum valle. Eia ergo, advocáta nostra, illos tuos misericórdes óculos ad nos convérte. Et Iesum, benedíctum fructum ventris tui, nobis post hoc exsílium osténde. O clemens, O pia, O dulcis Virgo María."},{id:"for-family",title:"For my family",tags:["family","evening","protection"],note:"Written for this app.",text:"Lord Jesus, you grew up in a home at Nazareth, in the care of Mary and Joseph. Bless my family. Give us patience with each other, and the grace to say sorry quickly and to forgive more quickly still. Keep those who are away from us, comfort those who are struggling, and bring each one of us home to you. Holy Family of Nazareth, pray for us. Amen."},{id:"for-children",title:"For my children and the young",tags:["family","children","protection","intercession"],note:"Written for this app.",text:"Father, these children are yours before they are mine. Keep them safe in body and in soul. Give them good friends, honest work, and a love for the truth. When they stray, bring them back; when they are afraid, be near. Help me to teach them more by my life than by my words. Through Christ our Lord. Amen."},{id:"before-decision",title:"Before a hard decision",tags:["decision","guidance","discernment","anxiety"],note:"Written for this app.",text:"Lord, I do not see clearly, and I am afraid of choosing wrongly. Quiet my fears and the voices that crowd your own. Show me what is true; show me what I am avoiding. Give me the courage to do what you ask, even if it costs me, and the peace to leave the rest in your hands. Whatever I decide, let it be for love of you. Amen."},{id:"before-work",title:"Before work",tags:["work","morning","offering"],note:"Written for this app.",text:"Lord, you worked with your hands at Nazareth and made all honest labor holy. Bless the work of this day. Keep me from carelessness and from the pride that cannot rest. Let me serve those who depend on me, treat everyone I meet with respect, and finish what I begin. May what I do today, small as it is, be an offering to you. Amen."},{id:"for-unemployed",title:"For those without work",tags:["work","trouble","need","intercession"],note:"Written for this app.",text:"God of Joseph the carpenter, look with mercy on all who are looking for work, and on those who are afraid of losing it. Give them courage when doors close, and open the right door at the right time. Provide for their families, and move us who have enough to help those who do not. Through Christ our Lord. Amen."},{id:"for-exams",title:"For students before an exam",tags:["study","anxiety","children"],note:"Written for this app.",text:"Holy Spirit, give me a clear mind and a steady heart. Help me remember what I have learned, keep me calm when I am nervous, and let me do my honest best. Whatever the result, help me to know that I am more than a grade. St Thomas Aquinas, pray for me. Amen."},{id:"for-the-suffering",title:"For a friend who is suffering",tags:["sick","intercession","trouble","need"],note:"Written for this app.",text:"Lord, you wept at the tomb of your friend. Be close to the one I bring to you now. I do not know how to fix this, and I cannot take away the pain; but you can be with them in it. Give them strength for today, and a friend to sit with them. Give me the grace to stay, and to be kind. Into your hands I place them. Amen."},{id:"for-forgiveness-of-others",title:"When I cannot forgive",tags:["forgiveness","confession","family","sorrow"],note:"Written for this app.",text:"Jesus, from the cross you forgave those who were killing you. I cannot do that yet. I am still angry, and I am hurt. Take what I have to give: my wish to wish them well. Bless the one who wronged me; heal what is broken in them and in me. Where I am not ready, be patient with me, and make me ready. Amen."},{id:"thanksgiving",title:"A prayer of thanksgiving",tags:["thanksgiving","praise","evening","daily"],note:"Written for this app.",text:"Father, thank you for this day and everything in it: for the food on the table, for the people who love me, for what went well and for what taught me something. Thank you for the gifts I did not notice until now. Teach me to receive each day as a gift, and to give thanks in all things. Glory be to you, now and always. Amen."},{id:"for-priests",title:"For priests",tags:["church","vocation","intercession","bishops"],note:"Written for this app.",text:"Lord Jesus, you are the one High Priest. Bless the priests who serve me and my family: the one who baptized us, who hears our confessions, and who gives us your Body. Keep them faithful, hold them in loneliness, and refresh them when they are tired. Send more priests, after your own heart. Mary, Mother of priests, pray for them. Amen."},{id:"for-the-unborn",title:"For unborn children and their mothers",tags:["life","family","intercession","need"],note:"Written for this app.",text:"Lord, author of life, you knit each child together in the womb. Protect the unborn, and surround every mother who is frightened with real help and real friends. Heal those who grieve a child they have lost, including those who regret a choice they made; there is mercy for them. Turn our hearts toward every human life. Amen."},{id:"night-prayer-short",title:"A short night prayer",tags:["evening","daily","protection","trust"],note:"Adapted from the Compline response; the words are Psalm 31:5 and Luke 23:46.",text:"Into thy hands, O Lord, I commend my spirit. Keep me as the apple of thine eye; hide me under the shadow of thy wings. Watch, O Lord, with those who wake or watch or weep tonight, and give thine angels charge over those who sleep. Amen."}],e="Written for this app.",o=[{id:"home-new",title:"Blessing of a new home",tags:["home","family","blessing"],note:e,text:"Lord God, you made your home among us. Bless this house and everyone who will live and visit here. Keep it a place of peace, where the door is open to the stranger, the table is shared, and your name is spoken with love. Let no anger last past the evening, and let every guest be welcomed as Christ. Through Christ our Lord. Amen."},{id:"home-epiphany",title:"Blessing the home at Epiphany (chalk)",tags:["home","epiphany","blessing","family"],note:"A traditional custom, with this prayer written for this app. Chalk the year over the main door with the letters C+M+B in the middle, for example 20+C+M+B+27. The letters stand for the names of the Magi and for “Christ bless this house”.",text:"Lord Jesus, the Magi found you in a house with Mary your mother. Come into this house as you came into theirs. Bless the door we mark today, and all who go in and out by it. Keep us from harm, make us your family, and lead us home to you at the end of our days. Amen."},{id:"home-evening-blessing",title:"A parent’s blessing for a child at bedtime",tags:["home","children","family","evening","blessing"],note:e,text:"Make the sign of the cross on the child’s forehead and say: “(Name), may God bless you and keep you. May Jesus be close to you tonight, may your angel watch over you, and may Mary your mother cover you with her mantle. In the name of the Father, and of the Son, and of the Holy Spirit. Amen.”"},{id:"home-pregnancy",title:"Blessing of a mother expecting a child",tags:["home","family","life","blessing","need"],note:e,text:"Lord God, you chose Mary to bear your Son. Look kindly on this mother and on the child she carries. Give her strength in these months, peace in her worry, and safe delivery in her time. Surround her family with care, and let the child be welcomed with joy, a gift from your hand. Through Christ our Lord. Amen."},{id:"home-birthday",title:"A birthday blessing",tags:["home","family","thanksgiving","blessing"],note:e,text:"Father, we thank you for the gift of (Name) and for another year of life. Bless the days ahead. Give (him/her) good health, true friends, and the courage to follow Christ. May the saint whose name (he/she) bears pray for (him/her) all the year. Amen."},{id:"meal-sunday",title:"Grace for Sunday dinner",tags:["home","meals","family","thanksgiving","blessing"],note:e,text:"Lord, today we remember your resurrection and we sit at table with joy. Bless this food and the hands that made it. Bless those who are not with us, and the hungry who have nothing to eat. Make us thankful, and make us generous. Amen."},{id:"meal-lent",title:"Grace in Lent",tags:["home","meals","lent","family","blessing"],note:e,text:"Lord, in these forty days we eat simply and thank you for all your gifts. Let our small sacrifices open our hearts to the poor. Bless this plain meal, and make us hungry for your Word. Amen."},{id:"meal-feast",title:"Grace on a feast day",tags:["home","meals","family","thanksgiving","blessing"],note:e,text:"Father, we keep this feast with gladness. Bless the table, the cook, and the company. Let our laughter be a sign of the joy of heaven, where the saints sit at your banquet without end. Amen."},{id:"meal-thanksgiving",title:"Grace for a national day of thanks",tags:["home","meals","family","thanksgiving","blessing"],note:e,text:"God of every nation and every harvest, we thank you for this food, this family and this land. Remember all who are away from home, who grieve, or who go without. Teach us to give as freely as we have received. Amen."},{id:"advent-wreath-1",title:"Advent wreath: first week",tags:["home","advent","family","blessing"],note:"Light one candle and read: “Be watchful: you do not know the day.” (Matthew 24:42)",text:"Lord Jesus, as we light the first candle we begin to wait. Wake our hearts from sleep, and make us ready to welcome you when you come. Amen."},{id:"advent-wreath-2",title:"Advent wreath: second week",tags:["home","advent","family","blessing"],note:"Light two candles and read: “Prepare the way of the Lord.” (Matthew 3:3)",text:"Lord Jesus, John the Baptist cried out in the desert. Help us to listen, to turn back from what holds us, and to straighten the road that leads to you. Amen."},{id:"advent-wreath-3",title:"Advent wreath: third week",tags:["home","advent","family","blessing"],note:"Light three candles, the rose one included, and read: “Rejoice in the Lord always.” (Philippians 4:4)",text:"Lord Jesus, the day is nearer. Give us the joy that does not depend on what we own, and let us share it with those who are sad. Amen."},{id:"advent-wreath-4",title:"Advent wreath: fourth week",tags:["home","advent","family","blessing"],note:"Light all four candles and read: “Behold, I am the handmaid of the Lord.” (Luke 1:38)",text:"Lord Jesus, Mary said yes and the Word became flesh. Help us to say yes to what you ask of us, and prepare a place for you in this home. Amen."},{id:"home-crib",title:"Blessing of the Christmas crib",tags:["home","christmas","family","blessing"],note:e,text:"Lord Jesus, you were born in a stable, laid in a manger, adored by shepherds and kings. Bless this crib. May it remind us each day that you came among the poor and that you are near. Amen."},{id:"home-easter-food",title:"Blessing of Easter food",tags:["home","easter","meals","family","blessing"],note:e,text:"Risen Lord, after the long fast we gather at your table. Bless this bread, these eggs, and everything we share on the day of your victory. As we eat together may we taste the joy of your resurrection, and long for the feast that never ends. Amen."},{id:"home-travel",title:"Before a journey",tags:["home","travel","family","protection","blessing"],note:e,text:"Lord, you walked every road with your people. Go with us now. Keep us safe from harm, bring us to our destination in peace, and bring us home again. Let your angels guard the way. Through Christ our Lord. Amen."},{id:"home-car",title:"Blessing of a car",tags:["home","travel","family","protection","blessing"],note:e,text:"Lord, bless this car and all who ride in it. Keep the driver alert and patient, the passengers peaceful, and everyone on the road safe. May every trip bring us where we need to go, and bring us home to you at last. Amen."},{id:"home-sick-child",title:"For a sick child",tags:["home","children","sick","family","need","blessing"],note:e,text:"Jesus, friend of children, you took them in your arms and blessed them. Look on (Name) now, who is sick. Ease the pain, quiet the fear, and bring healing in your own time. Hold the parents’ worry in your hands, and let us all trust you. Amen."},{id:"home-leaving",title:"When someone leaves home",tags:["home","family","blessing","protection"],note:e,text:"Father, (Name) is leaving home for school, for work, for a new place. Go before (him/her) and stay beside (him/her). Keep (him/her) close to you, give (him/her) good friends, and let (him/her) always know the way back. Amen."},{id:"home-peace-after-quarrel",title:"After a quarrel at home",tags:["home","family","forgiveness","peace","blessing"],note:e,text:"Lord, we hurt one another today, and we are sorry. Soften our hearts. Give us the grace to say the hard words, “I was wrong,” and “I forgive you.” Let the sun go down on peace in this house. Amen."},{id:"home-guests",title:"Welcoming guests",tags:["home","family","blessing","meals"],note:e,text:"Lord Jesus, you said that whoever welcomes a stranger welcomes you. Bless our guests as they come into our home, and let them leave with more peace than they brought. Amen."},{id:"home-absent-faith",title:"For a family member who has left the faith",tags:["home","family","intercession","need"],note:e,text:"Lord, you went after the one lost sheep. Hold (Name) in your love tonight. Where I have failed (him/her), forgive me. Where (he/she) is angry or hurt, heal. Bring (him/her) home in your time, and give me patience and gentleness while we wait. Amen."}],a=[{id:"sign",title:"Sign of the Cross",tags:["basic","morning","evening","daily"],text:"In the name of the Father, and of the Son, and of the Holy Spirit. Amen."},{id:"pater",title:"Our Father",tags:["basic","daily","lord"],text:"Our Father, who art in heaven, hallowed be thy name; thy kingdom come; thy will be done on earth as it is in heaven. Give us this day our daily bread; and forgive us our trespasses as we forgive those who trespass against us; and lead us not into temptation, but deliver us from evil. Amen."},{id:"ave",title:"Hail Mary",tags:["basic","mary","daily"],text:"Hail Mary, full of grace, the Lord is with thee; blessed art thou among women, and blessed is the fruit of thy womb, Jesus. Holy Mary, Mother of God, pray for us sinners, now and at the hour of our death. Amen."},{id:"gloria",title:"Glory Be",tags:["basic","trinity","daily"],text:"Glory be to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Spirit, as it was in the beginning, is now, and ever shall be, world without end. Amen."},{id:"creed",title:"Apostles’ Creed",tags:["basic","faith","creed"],text:"I believe in God, the Father almighty, Creator of heaven and earth; and in Jesus Christ, his only Son, our Lord, who was conceived by the Holy Ghost, born of the Virgin Mary, suffered under Pontius Pilate, was crucified, died and was buried; he descended into hell; on the third day he rose again from the dead; he ascended into heaven, and is seated at the right hand of God the Father almighty; from there he will come to judge the living and the dead. I believe in the Holy Ghost, the holy catholic Church, the communion of saints, the forgiveness of sins, the resurrection of the body, and life everlasting. Amen."},{id:"nicene",title:"Nicene Creed",tags:["faith","creed","mass","sunday","basic"],note:"The long-used traditional English wording (the pre-1970 Missal). The Creed as proclaimed at Mass today is the ICEL translation, which is copyrighted; the faith it professes is the same.",text:"I believe in one God, the Father Almighty, Maker of heaven and earth, and of all things visible and invisible. And in one Lord Jesus Christ, the only-begotten Son of God, born of the Father before all ages; God of God, Light of Light, true God of true God; begotten, not made; consubstantial with the Father, by whom all things were made. Who for us men and for our salvation came down from heaven, and was incarnate by the Holy Ghost of the Virgin Mary, and was made man. He was also crucified for us, suffered under Pontius Pilate, and was buried. And on the third day he rose again according to the Scriptures; and ascended into heaven, and sitteth at the right hand of the Father; and he shall come again with glory to judge the living and the dead; of whose kingdom there shall be no end. And in the Holy Ghost, the Lord and giver of life, who proceedeth from the Father and the Son; who together with the Father and the Son is adored and glorified; who spoke by the prophets. And one holy catholic and apostolic Church. I confess one baptism for the remission of sins. And I look for the resurrection of the dead, and the life of the world to come. Amen."},{id:"trisagion",title:"The Trisagion",tags:["eastern","praise","trinity","daily","byzantine"],note:"The thrice-holy hymn of the Eastern Churches, prayed at the start of most services.",text:"Holy God, Holy Mighty, Holy Immortal, have mercy on us. (Three times.) Glory to the Father and to the Son and to the Holy Spirit, now and ever and unto ages of ages. Amen."},{id:"heavenly-king",title:"O Heavenly King",tags:["eastern","holy-spirit","morning","daily","byzantine"],note:"The prayer to the Holy Spirit that opens the Byzantine day and its services.",text:"O Heavenly King, O Comforter, the Spirit of Truth, who art everywhere present and fillest all things, Treasury of blessings and Giver of life: come and abide in us, and cleanse us from every stain, and save our souls, O Good One."},{id:"pater-east",title:"Our Father, with the doxology",tags:["eastern","basic","daily","lord","byzantine"],note:"Prayed with the closing doxology in the Eastern Churches and many other traditions.",text:"Our Father, who art in heaven, hallowed be thy name; thy kingdom come; thy will be done on earth as it is in heaven. Give us this day our daily bread; and forgive us our trespasses as we forgive those who trespass against us; and lead us not into temptation, but deliver us from the evil one. For thine is the kingdom and the power and the glory, of the Father, and of the Son, and of the Holy Spirit, now and ever and unto ages of ages. Amen."},{id:"ephrem",title:"Prayer of St Ephrem",tags:["eastern","lent","repentance","byzantine","sorrow"],note:"Said throughout the Great Fast in the Byzantine tradition, with prostrations.",text:"O Lord and Master of my life, take from me the spirit of sloth, despair, lust of power and idle talk. But give rather the spirit of chastity, humility, patience and love to thy servant. Yea, O Lord and King, grant me to see my own transgressions and not to judge my brother, for blessed art thou unto ages of ages. Amen."},{id:"pascha-troparion",title:"The Paschal troparion",tags:["eastern","easter","praise","byzantine","pascha"],note:"Sung again and again from Pascha until the Ascension.",text:"Christ is risen from the dead, trampling down death by death, and upon those in the tombs bestowing life."},{id:"axion-est",title:"It is truly meet",tags:["eastern","mary","praise","byzantine","theotokos"],note:"The hymn to the Mother of God sung in the Divine Liturgy.",text:"It is truly meet to bless thee, O Theotokos, ever blessed and most pure, and the Mother of our God. More honorable than the Cherubim, and beyond compare more glorious than the Seraphim, without corruption thou gavest birth to God the Word: true Theotokos, we magnify thee."},{id:"nicene-east",title:"Nicene–Constantinopolitan Creed (Eastern form)",tags:["eastern","faith","creed","mass","sunday","byzantine"],note:"The Creed as the Eastern Churches say it, without the Latin addition “and the Son”. The faith professed is the same; the Catholic Church allows each its own form.",text:"I believe in one God, the Father Almighty, Maker of heaven and earth, and of all things visible and invisible. And in one Lord Jesus Christ, the only-begotten Son of God, begotten of the Father before all ages; Light of Light, true God of true God; begotten, not made; of one essence with the Father, by whom all things were made. Who for us men and for our salvation came down from heaven, and was incarnate of the Holy Spirit and the Virgin Mary, and became man. And was crucified for us under Pontius Pilate, and suffered, and was buried. And on the third day he rose again, according to the Scriptures. And ascended into heaven, and sitteth at the right hand of the Father. And he shall come again with glory to judge the living and the dead; whose kingdom shall have no end. And in the Holy Spirit, the Lord, the Giver of life, who proceedeth from the Father, who with the Father and the Son together is worshipped and glorified, who spoke by the prophets. In one holy, catholic and apostolic Church. I acknowledge one baptism for the remission of sins. I look for the resurrection of the dead, and the life of the world to come. Amen."},{id:"contrition",title:"Act of Contrition",tags:["confession","sorrow","forgiveness","evening","sin"],text:"O my God, I am heartily sorry for having offended thee, and I detest all my sins, because of thy just punishments, but most of all because they offend thee, my God, who art all good and deserving of all my love. I firmly resolve, with the help of thy grace, to sin no more and to avoid the near occasion of sin. Amen."},{id:"morning-offering",title:"Morning Offering",tags:["morning","daily","offering","work"],text:"O Jesus, through the Immaculate Heart of Mary, I offer thee my prayers, works, joys and sufferings of this day, for all the intentions of thy Sacred Heart, in union with the Holy Sacrifice of the Mass throughout the world, for the salvation of souls, the reparation of sins, the reunion of all Christians, and in particular for the intentions of the Holy Father this month. Amen."},{id:"guardian-angel",title:"Guardian Angel prayer",tags:["angels","children","protection","morning","evening","travel"],text:"Angel of God, my guardian dear, to whom God’s love commits me here, ever this day be at my side, to light and guard, to rule and guide. Amen."},{id:"michael",title:"Prayer to St Michael",tags:["angels","protection","spiritual-battle","temptation","fear"],text:"St Michael the Archangel, defend us in battle. Be our protection against the wickedness and snares of the devil. May God rebuke him, we humbly pray; and do thou, O Prince of the heavenly host, by the power of God, cast into hell Satan and all the evil spirits who prowl about the world seeking the ruin of souls. Amen."},{id:"memorare",title:"The Memorare",tags:["mary","intercession","need","trouble","family"],text:"Remember, O most gracious Virgin Mary, that never was it known that anyone who fled to thy protection, implored thy help, or sought thy intercession, was left unaided. Inspired by this confidence, I fly unto thee, O Virgin of virgins, my Mother; to thee do I come, before thee I stand, sinful and sorrowful. O Mother of the Word Incarnate, despise not my petitions, but in thy mercy hear and answer me. Amen."},{id:"salve",title:"Hail, Holy Queen",tags:["mary","evening","rosary","compline"],text:"Hail, holy Queen, Mother of mercy, our life, our sweetness and our hope. To thee do we cry, poor banished children of Eve; to thee do we send up our sighs, mourning and weeping in this valley of tears. Turn then, most gracious advocate, thine eyes of mercy toward us, and after this our exile, show unto us the blessed fruit of thy womb, Jesus. O clement, O loving, O sweet Virgin Mary."},{id:"magnificat",title:"The Magnificat",tags:["mary","thanksgiving","praise","evening","vespers"],note:"Luke 1:46-55, in the traditional Douay-Rheims wording.",text:"My soul doth magnify the Lord, and my spirit hath rejoiced in God my Saviour. Because he hath regarded the humility of his handmaid; for behold from henceforth all generations shall call me blessed. Because he that is mighty hath done great things to me; and holy is his name. And his mercy is from generation unto generations, to them that fear him. He hath showed might in his arm: he hath scattered the proud in the conceit of their heart. He hath put down the mighty from their seat, and hath exalted the humble. He hath filled the hungry with good things; and the rich he hath sent empty away. He hath received Israel his servant, being mindful of his mercy: as he spoke to our fathers, to Abraham and to his seed for ever."},{id:"come-holy-spirit",title:"Come, Holy Spirit",tags:["holy-spirit","guidance","study","decision","confirmation","pentecost","discernment"],text:"Come, Holy Spirit, fill the hearts of thy faithful and kindle in them the fire of thy love. V. Send forth thy Spirit and they shall be created. R. And thou shalt renew the face of the earth. Let us pray. O God, who didst instruct the hearts of the faithful by the light of the Holy Spirit, grant that by the same Spirit we may be truly wise and ever rejoice in his consolation, through Christ our Lord. Amen."},{id:"veni-creator",title:"Veni Creator Spiritus (excerpt)",tags:["holy-spirit","guidance","ordination","discernment"],text:"Come, Holy Ghost, Creator blest, and in our hearts take up thy rest; come with thy grace and heavenly aid, to fill the hearts which thou hast made. O Comforter, to thee we cry, thou heavenly gift of God most high, thou fount of life and fire of love, and sweet anointing from above."},{id:"anima-christi",title:"Anima Christi",tags:["eucharist","thanksgiving","communion","mass"],text:"Soul of Christ, sanctify me. Body of Christ, save me. Blood of Christ, inebriate me. Water from the side of Christ, wash me. Passion of Christ, strengthen me. O good Jesus, hear me. Within thy wounds hide me. Suffer me not to be separated from thee. From the malicious enemy defend me. In the hour of my death call me, and bid me come to thee, that with thy saints I may praise thee for ever and ever. Amen."},{id:"spiritual-communion",title:"Act of Spiritual Communion",tags:["eucharist","communion","sick","travel","mass"],text:"My Jesus, I believe that thou art present in the Most Blessed Sacrament. I love thee above all things, and I desire to receive thee into my soul. Since I cannot now receive thee sacramentally, come at least spiritually into my heart. I embrace thee as if thou wert already there, and unite myself wholly to thee. Never permit me to be separated from thee. Amen."},{id:"adoro-te",title:"Adoro Te Devote (first verse)",tags:["eucharist","adoration","communion","praise"],text:"Godhead here in hiding, whom I do adore, masked by these bare shadows, shape and nothing more, see, Lord, at thy service low lies here a heart lost, all lost in wonder at the God thou art."},{id:"tantum-ergo",title:"Tantum Ergo",tags:["eucharist","adoration","benediction","thursday"],text:"Down in adoration falling, this great Sacrament we hail; over ancient forms of worship, newer rites of grace prevail; faith will tell us Christ is present, when our human senses fail. To the everlasting Father, and the Son who reigns on high, with the Holy Ghost proceeding forth from each eternally, be salvation, honor, blessing, might and endless majesty. Amen."},{id:"before-meals",title:"Grace before meals",tags:["meals","family","thanksgiving","daily"],text:"Bless us, O Lord, and these thy gifts, which we are about to receive from thy bounty, through Christ our Lord. Amen."},{id:"after-meals",title:"Grace after meals",tags:["meals","family","thanksgiving","daily"],text:"We give thee thanks for all thy benefits, almighty God, who livest and reignest world without end. Amen. May the souls of the faithful departed, through the mercy of God, rest in peace. Amen."},{id:"serenity",title:"Prayer for serenity",tags:["anxiety","peace","trouble","decision","addiction"],note:"Often attributed to Reinhold Niebuhr; widely prayed.",text:"God, grant me the serenity to accept the things I cannot change, courage to change the things I can, and wisdom to know the difference. Amen."},{id:"st-francis",title:"Prayer attributed to St Francis",tags:["peace","service","morning","forgiveness"],note:"In this form the prayer dates from the early twentieth century; it is attributed to St Francis rather than written by him.",text:"Lord, make me an instrument of thy peace: where there is hatred, let me sow love; where there is injury, pardon; where there is doubt, faith; where there is despair, hope; where there is darkness, light; and where there is sadness, joy. O Divine Master, grant that I may not so much seek to be consoled as to console, to be understood as to understand, to be loved as to love. For it is in giving that we receive, it is in pardoning that we are pardoned, and it is in dying that we are born to eternal life. Amen."},{id:"jesus-prayer",title:"The Jesus Prayer",tags:["quiet","anxiety","sorrow","daily","breath"],text:"Lord Jesus Christ, Son of God, have mercy on me, a sinner."},{id:"psalm-23",title:"Psalm 22 (23), The Lord is my shepherd",tags:["comfort","fear","grief","trust","sick","funeral"],note:"Douay-Rheims numbering. Read it in your own translation on the Bible tab at Psalm 23.",text:"The Lord ruleth me, and I shall want nothing. He hath set me in a place of pasture. He hath brought me up, on the water of refreshment: he hath converted my soul. He hath led me on the paths of justice, for his own name’s sake. For though I should walk in the midst of the shadow of death, I will fear no evils, for thou art with me. Thy rod and thy staff, they have comforted me. Thou hast prepared a table before me against them that afflict me. Thou hast fattened my head with oil; and my chalice which inebriateth me, how goodly is it! And thy mercy will follow me all the days of my life. And that I may dwell in the house of the Lord, unto length of days."},{id:"psalm-50",title:"Psalm 50 (51), Miserere",tags:["confession","sorrow","forgiveness","lent","sin","repentance"],note:"Douay-Rheims numbering.",text:"Have mercy on me, O God, according to thy great mercy. And according to the multitude of thy tender mercies blot out my iniquity. Wash me yet more from my iniquity, and cleanse me from my sin. For I know my iniquity, and my sin is always before me. Create a clean heart in me, O God: and renew a right spirit within my bowels. Cast me not away from thy face; and take not thy holy spirit from me. Restore unto me the joy of thy salvation, and strengthen me with a perfect spirit."},{id:"de-profundis",title:"De Profundis (Psalm 129)",tags:["dead","purgatory","grief","funeral","november","sorrow"],note:"Douay-Rheims numbering (Psalm 130 in modern Bibles).",text:"Out of the depths I have cried to thee, O Lord: Lord, hear my voice. Let thy ears be attentive to the voice of my supplication. If thou, O Lord, wilt mark iniquities: Lord, who shall endure it? For with thee there is merciful forgiveness: and by reason of thy law, I have waited for thee, O Lord. My soul hath relied on his word: my soul hath hoped in the Lord. From the morning watch even until night, let Israel hope in the Lord. Because with the Lord there is mercy: and with him plentiful redemption. And he shall redeem Israel from all his iniquities."},{id:"eternal-rest",title:"Eternal rest",tags:["dead","purgatory","grief","funeral","november","meals"],text:"Eternal rest grant unto them, O Lord, and let perpetual light shine upon them. May they rest in peace. Amen."},{id:"st-joseph",title:"Prayer to St Joseph",tags:["joseph","work","family","fathers","workers","happy-death","intercession"],text:"To thee, O blessed Joseph, we have recourse in our affliction, and having implored the help of thy most holy Spouse, we confidently invoke thy patronage also. Through that charity which bound thee to the Immaculate Virgin Mother of God, and through the paternal love with which thou didst embrace the Child Jesus, we humbly beseech thee to look graciously upon the inheritance which Jesus Christ has purchased by his Blood, and to help us in our needs by thy power and strength. Amen."},{id:"st-anthony",title:"Prayer to St Anthony",tags:["lost","intercession","finding","anthony"],text:"Holy St Anthony, gentlest of saints, your love for God and charity for his creatures made you worthy, when on earth, to possess miraculous powers. Miracles waited on your word, which you were ever ready to speak for those in trouble or anxiety. Encouraged by this thought, I implore you to obtain for me the favour I seek in this prayer. Amen."},{id:"st-ignatius-suscipe",title:"Suscipe of St Ignatius",tags:["surrender","offering","discernment","trust","jesuit"],text:"Take, Lord, and receive all my liberty, my memory, my understanding, and my entire will, all that I have and possess. You have given all to me. To you, Lord, I return it. All is yours; dispose of it according to your will. Give me only your love and your grace, for this is enough for me."},{id:"before-study",title:"Prayer of St Thomas Aquinas before study",tags:["study","students","wisdom","exams","bible"],text:"Ineffable Creator, who out of the treasures of thy wisdom hast appointed three hierarchies of angels and set them in wondrous order above the heavens, and hast distributed the portions of the universe in most skilful array, thou who art called the true fountain of light and wisdom, and the all-transcending beginning, be pleased to shed upon the darkness of my mind, in which I was born, the twofold ray of thy brightness, to remove from me all the darkness of sin and ignorance. Amen."},{id:"opening-scripture",title:"Before reading Scripture",tags:["bible","study","lectio","word"],text:"Lord Jesus, open the Scriptures to us, as thou didst to the disciples on the road to Emmaus, and let our hearts burn within us as thou speakest. Amen."},{id:"evening-examen",title:"Evening prayer",tags:["evening","night","thanksgiving","daily"],text:"Visit, we beseech thee, O Lord, this dwelling, and drive far from it the snares of the enemy; let thy holy angels dwell herein to preserve us in peace, and let thy blessing be always upon us. Through Christ our Lord. Amen."},{id:"for-sick",title:"For the sick",tags:["sick","healing","illness","hospital","suffering"],text:"Lord Jesus Christ, who didst go about doing good and healing every sickness, look with mercy upon thy servant who is ill. Grant relief to his or her pain, strength in weakness, and the peace of knowing that thou art near. Give courage to those who care, and wisdom to those who heal. Whatever thy will, let us trust in thy love. Amen."},{id:"for-dying",title:"Prayer for a happy death",tags:["dying","dead","happy-death","joseph","sick"],text:"O Lord Jesus Christ, grant me by thy grace to die in thy friendship, strengthened by the sacraments of thy Church, with thy name upon my lips and in my heart. Mary, Mother of mercy, and Joseph, patron of a happy death, pray for us now and at the hour of our death. Amen."},{id:"travel",title:"Prayer for a journey",tags:["travel","journey","protection","angels"],text:"Lord, protect us on our way, and bring us safely to our destination. Send thy holy angel to guard and guide us, that we may travel in peace and return in joy. Through Christ our Lord. Amen."},{id:"for-vocation",title:"For vocations",tags:["vocation","priests","discernment","church"],text:"Lord of the harvest, send laborers into thy harvest. Give to the young the courage to answer thy call, to families the generosity to offer their children, and to all of us the readiness to say, with Mary, “Be it done unto me according to thy word.” Amen."},{id:"peace",title:"For peace",tags:["peace","war","world","church","justice"],text:"O God, from whom all holy desires, all good counsels and all just works do proceed: give unto thy servants that peace which the world cannot give, that our hearts may be set to obey thy commandments, and that, being defended from the fear of our enemies, we may pass our time in rest and quietness. Through Christ our Lord. Amen."},{id:"pope",title:"For the Pope and the Church",tags:["church","pope","intercession","bishops"],text:"Let us pray for our Pope. May the Lord preserve him, give him life, make him blessed upon the earth, and deliver him not up to the will of his enemies. Our Father, Hail Mary. Almighty and everlasting God, have mercy upon thy servant our Pope, and direct him according to thy loving kindness in the way of everlasting salvation, that of thy gift he may desire what is pleasing to thee and perform it with all his strength. Through Christ our Lord. Amen."}],i=[...a,...t,...o];export{i as B};
